://api.github.com/users/kim-vde","html_url":"https://github.com/kim-vde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/662488715","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7579#issuecomment-662488715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7579","id":662488715,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY2MjQ4ODcxNQ==","user":{"login":"emilieroberts","id":8290920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTA5MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8290920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts","html_url":"https://github.com/emilieroberts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-22T14:32:47Z","updated_at":"2020-07-22T14:32:47Z","body":"I believe so. I am extending ExoPlayer's MediaCodecVideoRenderer implementation so I assume that at some point the buffers must be non-null, since the video data comes out fine and is displayed.\r\n\r\nOn Kotlin, there is a runtime null check on values not declared nullable so it crashes when the null value comes in. If I disable the check, everything runs fine, and the video is shown, I don't see any dropped frames. To me this indicates that a null buffer must be used (or ignored) intentionally by Exo / MediaCodecVideoRenderer in some cases. In this case, when a Chromebook is used.\r\n\r\nWe could add a specific check in the code [here](https://github.com/chromeos/video-decode-encode-demo/blob/master/app/src/main/java/dev/hadrosaur/videodecodeencodedemo/VideoHelpers/VideoMediaCodecVideoRenderer.kt#L81) and log when/why a null buffer is passed in.\r\n\r\nI would assume the same to be true for MediaCodecAudioRenderer but have not tested.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/662488715/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"emilieroberts","id":8290920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTA5MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8290920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts","html_url":"https://github.com/emilieroberts","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilieroberts/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/662512729","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7579#issuecomment-662512729","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/7579","id":662512729,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDY2MjUxMjcyOQ==","user":{"login":"kim-vde","id":54320150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzIwMTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54320150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde","html_url":"https://github.com/kim-vde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-07-22T15:14:28Z","updated_at":"2020-07-22T15:14:28Z","body":"Actually, the buffer could be null in some cases (see [`MediaCodec#getOutputBuffer(int)`](https://developer.android.com/reference/android/media/MediaCodec#getOutputBuffer(int))). It is also not surprising to be able to play the video even if the buffers are null because `MediaCodecVideoRenderer#processOutputBuffer()` doesn't use the `buffer` parameter.\r\n\r\n> We could add a specific check in the code [here](https://github.com/chromeos/video-decode-encode-demo/blob/master/app/src/main/java/dev/hadrosaur/videodecodeencodedemo/VideoHelpers/VideoMediaCodecVideoRenderer.kt#L81) and log when/why a null buffer is passed in.\r\n\r\nThis would be interesting input for us to know whether the buffer being null is expected or whether this is a bug in the Chrome OS.\r\n\r\n> I would assume the same to be true for MediaCodecAudioRenderer but have not tested.\r\n\r\nThis would also be interesting to know if you have time to check.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/662512729/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"kim-vde","id":54320150,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0MzIwMTUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54320150?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde","html_url":"https://github.com/kim-vde","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kim-vde/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":3583296089,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDM1ODMyOTYwODk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/events/3583296089","actor":{"log